subproblem.statement:
Let n, N ∈ ℕ and write ℝᵏ := EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin k). Let ψ : ℝⁿ → ℝᴺ, x₀ ∈ ℝⁿ, c : ℝ → ℝⁿ, γ : ℝ → ℝᴺ and v ∈ ℝᴺ. Assume:
(i) ψ is Fréchet differentiable at x₀;
(ii) A := Dψ(x₀) = fderiv ℝ ψ x₀ is injective;
(iii) c(t) → x₀ as t → 0 along the full, unpunctured neighbourhood filter of 0 (Tendsto c (𝓝 0) (𝓝 x₀)); in particular c(0) = x₀ and c is continuous at 0;
(iv) γ(t) = ψ(c(t)) for all t in some neighbourhood of 0;
(v) γ has derivative v at 0.
Then v ∈ range A, i.e. v = A ζ for some ζ ∈ ℝⁿ (v ∈ LinearMap.range (fderiv ℝ ψ x₀).toLinearMap). No differentiability of c is assumed.
